From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Er Gibbio <gibbio@pm.me>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 15:28:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 23/23] display: leave the session clock out of own-clock
 stream reports

On its own clock, video reported the later of the session-clock margin
and the margin the default delay gives (0016). While audio plays the
session clock runs the audio's delay behind, so the session-clock margin
is about that delay and follows the audio buffer: ~140 ms, 186 after a
Wi-Fi pause grew the buffer, ~235 for a moment as the audio started.
spice-server's GStreamer rate control judges each report against the
largest one the stream has had: it lowered the bit rate twice as the
audio started and halved it at the pause, within 6 minutes (74 to 15.6
Mbit/s as a limit; the stream used ~3.8), and does not raise the limit
while the stream uses less than it.

Report only the default delay's margin there, as without audio: at most
50 ms, lower for a frame shown sooner than the target.
---
 src/channel-display.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/channel-display.c b/src/channel-display.c
index f428699..334810d 100644
--- a/src/channel-display.c
+++ b/src/channel-display.c
@@ -2271,7 +2271,11 @@ static void display_handle_stream_data(SpiceChannel *channel, SpiceMsgIn *in)
      *   its slack: a viewer's choice of target (Video Delay) and a frame that
      *   came early are no news. Uncapped, ~150 ms during a stream's first
      *   second, then 50, took H.264 to ~0.1 Mbit/s and 3 fps within a minute;
-     *   a change from 80 to 30 ms halved the bit rate;
+     *   a change from 80 to 30 ms halved the bit rate. Nor does the session
+     *   clock count there: while audio plays it runs the audio's delay behind,
+     *   and its margin follows the audio buffer (~140 ms, 186 after a Wi-Fi
+     *   pause grew it): reported, it lowered the bit rate twice as the audio
+     *   started and halved it at the pause, within 6 minutes;
      * - following the audio, the margin is about the audio's delay, which
      *   changes with the output device (~280 ms with AirPods, ~130 built in)
      *   and peaks for a moment when it does: from 408 to 131 ms, the server
@@ -2282,7 +2286,7 @@ static void display_handle_stream_data(SpiceChannel *channel, SpiceMsgIn *in)
     if (st->video_decoder->codec_type == SPICE_VIDEO_CODEC_TYPE_MJPEG) {
         server_margin = MAX(margin_report, margin);
     } else if (c->playout_target > 0 && !c->playout_audio) {
-        server_margin = MAX(margin_report, MIN(margin - c->playout_target, 0) + PLAYOUT_DEFAULT_MS);
+        server_margin = MIN(margin - c->playout_target, 0) + PLAYOUT_DEFAULT_MS;
     } else {
         server_margin = MIN(MAX(margin_report, margin), PLAYOUT_DEFAULT_MS);
         /* a frame late by no more than the decoder still shows is no drop */
